#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Render layered instruction files, install a layered agent setup, and detect drift in either.

  governance render   --out FILE [--core DIR] [--adapter DIR ...] [--local FILE]
  governance check    --out FILE [--core DIR] [--adapter DIR ...] [--local FILE]
  governance install  --home DIR --adapter DIR [--adapter DIR ...] [--local FILE]
                      [--harness claude|codex|grok ...] [--repo DIR] [--dry-run]
  governance check    --home DIR
  governance restore  --home DIR [--backup TIMESTAMP]
  governance discover --root DIR [--home DIR] [--max-depth N] [--write]
  governance reconcile --home DIR [--manifest FILE] [--dry-run] [--json]

RENDER. Layers are concatenated CORE → ADAPTER(s), in the order given → LOCAL, so on conflict the later
layer is the one a model reads last. Within a directory layer, AGENTS.md comes first, then every other
Markdown file in sorted path order. --core defaults to this repository's core/ directory.

Why render rather than link: symlinked instruction files and imports resolving outside the working
directory are skipped by some harness surfaces, silently. A rendered file loads everywhere; its only
failure mode is staleness, and `check` detects that.

The rendered file begins with a header carrying the sha256 of its body. `check` distinguishes the two
ways a rendered file goes wrong, because they have different fixes:
  LAYERS CHANGED   a layer was edited after rendering      → re-render
  EDITED BY HAND   the rendered file itself was edited      → move the edit into a layer, re-render

INSTALL builds a harness home from CORE (--repo, default this repository) and each ADAPTER directory.
--home is required and never defaults: pass --home "$HOME" to install for real. For --harness claude
(the default), under <home>/.claude/:
  CLAUDE.md               rendered: core/AGENTS.md → each adapter AGENTS.md → --local
  governance/<domain>.md  rendered: core/domains/<domain>.md → each adapter domains/<domain>.md
  skills/ hooks/ agents/ bin/
                          real directories holding one symlink per entry, core first, then adapters;
                          a later layer wins a name collision and the collision is reported — except
                          that no adapter may shadow a core hook: those are the floor
  scheduled-tasks         symlink to the one adapter that provides scheduled-tasks/ (two = refused)
  settings.json           deep merge of settings/claude.json, core then adapters: objects merge,
                          lists union in order, scalars take the later value. A layer can extend a
                          list or object but never replace it, so core deny rules and hook wiring
                          survive every adapter; disableAllHooks is refused outright.
--harness codex renders <home>/.codex/AGENTS.md; --harness grok renders
<home>/.grok/rules/00-governance.md and assembles <home>/.grok/skills/ like the claude skills.
The harness list is declarative: a re-install without a harness removes that harness's outputs.

UNDO FIRST. Before anything is touched, the prior state of every path the install will change — missing,
symlink → target, regular file, directory — is written to <home>/.governance-backup/<UTC timestamp>/
manifest.json, and existing files and directories are moved into that backup, never deleted. A
re-install that changes nothing writes no backup. `restore` (default: the newest backup) puts every path
back exactly; `restore --backup T` undoes every install from the newest back to T, so the home returns
to its state before T. <home>/.governance-state.json records the invocation, every rendered source
(path + sha256), and every output (path + type + sha256 or target).

CHECK --home re-derives the install from the recorded invocation and reports each output:
  in sync
  LAYERS CHANGED   a source changed, or an output was added or dropped   → re-install
  EDITED BY HAND   a rendered file differs from what was installed      → move the edit into a layer
  LINK MOVED       a symlink points somewhere else                       → re-install
  MISSING          an output is gone                                     → re-install

DISCOVER lists, read-only, the git repositories and vaults (directories holding .obsidian/ or a root
GOVERNANCE.md) under --root and which directories look like adapters (AGENTS.md plus any of skills/
hooks/ domains/ settings/). Each vault is classified: `adapter` when it holds .governance/AGENTS.md (the
organisation's layer lives INSIDE its knowledge vault, hidden from the vault UI, tracked by its git),
otherwise `member`. With --home it also proposes the MANIFEST — the machine-local record of what this
machine's setup should be — and with --write writes it to <home>/.governance/manifest.json. Two adapter
vaults under one root are refused: one machine has one organisation layer.

RECONCILE reads the manifest and ensures, in order, reporting one line per item as `ok` (already right,
nothing written) / `fixed` (changed) / `refused` (cannot be fixed safely):
  a. adapter shape      <adapter>/AGENTS.md exists (created from adapter-template/ if not); optional parts
                        (skills/ hooks/ agents/ bin/ domains/ settings/ scheduled-tasks/), if present, are dirs
  b. home               the install for the manifest's harnesses, adapter and local — a noop when in state
  c. GOVERNANCE.md      in every vault: frontmatter keys type/canonical_home/adapter/role and a pointer
                        block between <!-- governance:begin --> and <!-- governance:end -->; nothing else
                        in the file is touched, byte for byte
  d. CLAUDE.md          in every vault: the line `@GOVERNANCE.md` exactly once (appended if absent)
  e. drift              `check --home` over the result
Running it again when everything is in state changes nothing — no backup, no rewrite. --dry-run says
what would change and writes nothing. `install --write-manifest` seeds the manifest from its arguments so
the first install is the last command that needs any.

Exit: 0 done / in sync · 1 drift, or reconcile refused an item · 2 cannot run (a named layer or source
      is missing, the output is absent or has no header, the install was refused, there is nothing to
      restore, or there is no manifest)
"""
import argparse, datetime, hashlib, json, os, re, shutil, sys

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))  # realpath: bin/ is installed as a symlink
HEADER = "<!-- rendered by governance — DO NOT EDIT: change a layer, then re-render. sha256={} -->\n"
HEADER_RX = re.compile(r"\A<!-- rendered by governance — DO NOT EDIT: change a layer, then re-render\. sha256=([0-9a-f]{64}) -->\n")
STATE = ".governance-state.json"
BACKUPS = ".governance-backup"
BACKUP_RX = re.compile(r"\A\d{8}T\d{6}-\d{6}Z\Z")
MANIFEST = os.path.join(".governance", "manifest.json")
ADAPTER_DIR = ".governance"          # the organisation layer, inside its vault
ADAPTER_PARTS = ("skills", "hooks", "agents", "bin", "domains", "settings", "scheduled-tasks")
GOV_MD, CLAUDE_MD, IMPORT_LINE = "GOVERNANCE.md", "CLAUDE.md", "@GOVERNANCE.md"
MARK_BEGIN, MARK_END = "<!-- governance:begin -->", "<!-- governance:end -->"
HARNESSES = ("claude", "codex", "grok")
LINKED_PARTS = ("skills", "hooks", "agents", "bin")
DISCOVER_SKIP = {"node_modules", "__pycache__", "venv"}


class Refusal(Exception):
    """The inputs cannot be installed as given. Raised before anything is written."""


# --- rendering -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def layer_files(path):
    if os.path.isfile(path):
        return [(os.path.basename(path), path)]
    found = []
    for d, _, fs in os.walk(path):
        for f in fs:
            if f.endswith(".md"):
                full = os.path.join(d, f)
                found.append((os.path.relpath(full, path), full))
    found.sort(key=lambda rel_full: (rel_full[0] != "AGENTS.md", rel_full[0]))
    return found


def build_body(layers):
    parts = []
    for name, path in layers:
        for rel, full in layer_files(path):
            with open(full, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                text = fh.read()
            if not text.endswith("\n"):
                text += "\n"
            parts.append(f"<!-- layer: {name} · {rel} -->\n{text}")
    return "\n".join(parts)


def sha(text):
    return hashlib.sha256(text.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()


def file_sha(path):
    h = hashlib.sha256()
    with open(path, "rb") as fh:
        for chunk in iter(lambda: fh.read(65536), b""):
            h.update(chunk)
    return h.hexdigest()


def adapter_label(i, n):
    return "adapter" if n == 1 else f"adapter {i}"


def cmd_render_or_check_out(a):
    core = a.core or os.path.join(ROOT, "core")
    layers = [("core", core)] + [(adapter_label(i, len(a.adapter)), p) for i, p in enumerate(a.adapter, 1)] + \
             ([("local", a.local)] if a.local else [])
    for name, path in layers:
        if not os.path.exists(path):
            print(f"error: {name} layer not found: {path}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    body = build_body(layers)
    if not body:
        print("error: the layers contain no Markdown — refusing to render an empty instruction file",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    if a.command == "render":
        tmp = a.out + ".tmp"
        with open(tmp, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(HEADER.format(sha(body)) + body)
        os.replace(tmp, a.out)
        print(f"rendered {len(layers)} layer(s) → {a.out}")
        return 0

    if not os.path.isfile(a.out):
        print(f"NOT RENDERED  {a.out} does not exist", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    with open(a.out, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        current = fh.read()
    m = HEADER_RX.match(current)
    if not m:
        print(f"NOT RENDERED  {a.out} has no governance header — it was not produced by render",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    recorded, on_disk = m.group(1), current[m.end():]
    if sha(on_disk) != recorded:
        print(f"EDITED BY HAND  {a.out} — move the change into a layer, then re-render")
        return 1
    if recorded != sha(body):
        print(f"LAYERS CHANGED  {a.out} is stale — re-render")
        return 1
    print(f"in sync  {a.out}")
    return 0


# --- the install plan: what the home should contain, derived from the layers alone ----------------

class Plan:
    def __init__(self):
        self.outputs = {}   # home-relative path → wanted state; a parent always precedes its children
        self.sources = {}   # every file whose content is baked into an output → sha256
        self.notes = []

    def dir(self, rel):
        self.outputs.setdefault(rel, {"type": "dir"})

    def file(self, rel, text):
        self.outputs[rel] = {"type": "file", "sha256": sha(text), "text": text}

    def link(self, rel, target):
        self.outputs[rel] = {"type": "symlink", "target": target}

    def render(self, layers):
        for _, path in layers:
            self.sources.setdefault(path, file_sha(path))
        body = build_body(layers)
        return HEADER.format(sha(body)) + body


def record(rel, out):
    r = {"path": rel, "type": out["type"]}
    if out["type"] == "file":
        r["sha256"] = out["sha256"]
    elif out["type"] == "symlink":
        r["target"] = out["target"]
    return r


def md_names(d):
    return [f for f in sorted(os.listdir(d)) if f.endswith(".md") and os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, f))] \
        if os.path.isdir(d) else []


def link_sources(layers, part, notes):
    chosen = {}
    for name, parts_root, _ in layers:
        d = os.path.join(parts_root, part)
        if not os.path.isdir(d):
            continue
        for entry in sorted(os.listdir(d)):
            src = os.path.join(d, entry)
            wanted = os.path.isdir(src) if part == "skills" else os.path.isfile(src)
            if entry.startswith(".") or not wanted:
                continue
            if entry in chosen:
                prev = chosen[entry][0]
                if part == "hooks" and prev == "core":
                    raise Refusal(f"{name} provides hooks/{entry}, which would replace a core floor hook "
                                  f"({d}) — give it another name")
                notes.append(f"COLLISION  {part}/{entry}: {prev} overridden by {name} ({src})")
            chosen[entry] = (name, src)
    return {entry: src for entry, (_, src) in chosen.items()}


def merge(base, over, where, layer):
    if isinstance(base, dict) and isinstance(over, dict):
        out = dict(base)
        for k, v in over.items():
            out[k] = merge(base[k], v, f"{where}.{k}" if where else k, layer) if k in base else v
        return out
    if isinstance(base, list) and isinstance(over, list):
        out = list(base)
        for item in over:
            if item not in out:
                out.append(item)
        return out
    if isinstance(base, (dict, list)) or isinstance(over, (dict, list)):
        raise Refusal(f"{layer} settings: `{where}` is a {type(over).__name__} where an earlier layer has a "
                      f"{type(base).__name__} — a layer can extend a list or an object, never replace it")
    return over


def merged_settings(plan, layers):
    merged = {}
    for name, parts_root, _ in layers:
        p = os.path.join(parts_root, "settings", "claude.json")
        if not os.path.isfile(p):
            continue
        try:
            with open(p, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                data = json.load(fh)
        except ValueError as e:
            raise Refusal(f"{name} settings are not valid JSON: {p}: {e}")
        if not isinstance(data, dict):
            raise Refusal(f"{name} settings must be a JSON object: {p}")
        plan.sources.setdefault(p, file_sha(p))
        merged = merge(merged, data, "", name)
    if merged.get("disableAllHooks"):
        raise Refusal("the merged settings set disableAllHooks, which switches off the floor hooks — no layer may")
    return json.dumps(merged, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n"


def build_plan(repo, adapters, local, harnesses):
    if not os.path.isdir(repo):
        raise Refusal(f"core repository not found: {repo}")
    core_agents = os.path.join(repo, "core", "AGENTS.md")
    if not os.path.isfile(core_agents):
        raise Refusal(f"core instruction file not found: {core_agents}")
    # (name, root of skills/hooks/agents/bin/settings/scheduled-tasks, root of AGENTS.md and domains/)
    layers = [("core", repo, os.path.join(repo, "core"))]
    for i, a in enumerate(adapters, 1):
        if not os.path.isdir(a):
            raise Refusal(f"adapter not found: {a}")
        layers.append((adapter_label(i, len(adapters)), a, a))
    if local and not os.path.isfile(local):
        raise Refusal(f"local layer not found: {local}")

    plan = Plan()
    instruction = plan.render(
        [(n, os.path.join(ir, "AGENTS.md")) for n, _, ir in layers if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(ir, "AGENTS.md"))]
        + ([("local", local)] if local else []))
    providers = [(n, os.path.join(pr, "scheduled-tasks")) for n, pr, _ in layers[1:]
                 if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(pr, "scheduled-tasks"))]
    if len(providers) > 1:
        raise Refusal("scheduled-tasks is provided by more than one adapter ("
                      + ", ".join(f"{n}: {p}" for n, p in providers) + ") — at most one may provide it")
    parts = LINKED_PARTS if "claude" in harnesses else ("skills",) if "grok" in harnesses else ()
    links = {part: link_sources(layers, part, plan.notes) for part in parts}

    for h in harnesses:
        if h == "claude":
            plan.dir(".claude")
            plan.file(".claude/CLAUDE.md", instruction)
            plan.dir(".claude/governance")
            for d in sorted({d for _, _, ir in layers for d in md_names(os.path.join(ir, "domains"))}):
                plan.file(f".claude/governance/{d}", plan.render(
                    [(n, os.path.join(ir, "domains", d)) for n, _, ir in layers
                     if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(ir, "domains", d))]))
            for part in LINKED_PARTS:
                plan.dir(f".claude/{part}")
                for entry, src in links[part].items():
                    plan.link(f".claude/{part}/{entry}", src)
            if providers:
                plan.link(".claude/scheduled-tasks", providers[0][1])
            plan.file(".claude/settings.json", merged_settings(plan, layers))
        elif h == "codex":
            plan.dir(".codex")
            plan.file(".codex/AGENTS.md", instruction)
        elif h == "grok":
            plan.dir(".grok")
            plan.dir(".grok/rules")
            plan.file(".grok/rules/00-governance.md", instruction)
            plan.dir(".grok/skills")
            for entry, src in links["skills"].items():
                plan.link(f".grok/skills/{entry}", src)
    return plan


# --- the home as it is -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

def inspect(home, rel):
    """The current state of home/rel, never looking through an ancestor that is not a real directory:
    under a symlinked skills/ the entries belong to wherever it points, not to this home."""
    parts = rel.split("/")
    for i in range(2, len(parts)):
        anc = os.path.join(home, *parts[:i])
        if os.path.islink(anc) or not os.path.isdir(anc):
            return {"type": "missing"}
    p = os.path.join(home, rel)
    if os.path.islink(p):
        return {"type": "symlink", "target": os.readlink(p)}
    if os.path.isdir(p):
        return {"type": "dir"}
    if os.path.isfile(p):
        return {"type": "file", "sha256": file_sha(p)}
    return {"type": "unsupported"} if os.path.lexists(p) else {"type": "missing"}


def matches(home, rel, want, cur):
    if want["type"] == "dir":
        # A harness directory (~/.claude itself) may legitimately be a symlink to a directory.
        return cur["type"] == "dir" or ("/" not in rel and cur["type"] == "symlink"
                                        and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(home, rel)))
    if want["type"] == "file":
        return cur["type"] == "file" and cur["sha256"] == want["sha256"]
    return cur["type"] == "symlink" and cur["target"] == want["target"]


def load_state(home):
    p = os.path.join(home, STATE)
    if not os.path.isfile(p):
        return None
    try:
        with open(p, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            return json.load(fh)
    except ValueError as e:
        raise Refusal(f"cannot read {p}: {e}")


# --- install ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def plan_changes(home, plan, invocation):
    old = load_state(home)
    changes, notes = [], []
    stale = [o["path"] for o in (old or {}).get("outputs", []) if o["path"] not in plan.outputs]
    for rel in sorted(stale, key=lambda r: -r.count("/")):   # children before their directory
        cur = inspect(home, rel)
        if cur["type"] == "missing":
            continue
        if cur["type"] == "unsupported":
            raise Refusal(f"{os.path.join(home, rel)} is neither a file, a directory nor a symlink")
        if cur["type"] == "dir":
            leaving = {c[0].rsplit("/", 1)[1] for c in changes if c[0].rsplit("/", 1)[0] == rel}
            if "/" not in rel or set(os.listdir(os.path.join(home, rel))) - leaving:
                notes.append(f"left in place (no longer installed, holds other files): {os.path.join(home, rel)}")
                continue
        changes.append((rel, cur, None))
    for rel, want in plan.outputs.items():
        cur = inspect(home, rel)
        if cur["type"] == "unsupported":
            raise Refusal(f"{os.path.join(home, rel)} is neither a file, a directory nor a symlink")
        if not matches(home, rel, want, cur):
            changes.append((rel, cur, want))
    state = {"version": 1, "invocation": invocation,
             "sources": [{"path": p, "sha256": s} for p, s in plan.sources.items()],
             "outputs": [record(r, o) for r, o in plan.outputs.items()]}
    text = json.dumps(state, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n"
    want = {"type": "file", "sha256": sha(text), "text": text}
    cur = inspect(home, STATE)
    if not matches(home, STATE, want, cur):
        changes.append((STATE, cur, want))
    return changes, notes


def describe(rel, cur, want):
    if want is None:
        return f"remove   {rel}"
    if cur["type"] == "missing":
        return f"create   {rel}"
    return f"replace  {rel} (was {cur['type']})"


def new_backup(home):
    while True:
        name = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y%m%dT%H%M%S-%fZ")
        path = os.path.join(home, BACKUPS, name)
        try:
            os.makedirs(path)
            return name, path
        except FileExistsError:
            continue


def write_json(path, data):
    tmp = path + ".tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        json.dump(data, fh, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)
        fh.write("\n")
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def create(p, want):
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)
    if want["type"] == "dir":
        os.mkdir(p)
    elif want["type"] == "symlink":
        os.symlink(want["target"], p)
    else:
        tmp = p + ".governance-tmp"
        with open(tmp, "wb") as fh:
            fh.write(want["text"].encode("utf-8"))
        os.replace(tmp, p)


def install_home(home, invocation, dry_run=False, say=print):
    """Bring HOME to the state the invocation implies. Returns (exit code, number of changes applied
    or, on a dry run, that would be applied). A home already in state gets no backup and no write."""
    try:
        plan = build_plan(invocation["repo"], invocation["adapters"], invocation["local"], invocation["harnesses"])
        changes, notes = plan_changes(home, plan, invocation)
    except Refusal as e:
        print(f"refused: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2, 0
    for n in plan.notes + notes:
        say(n)
    override = os.path.join(home, ".codex", "AGENTS.override.md")
    if "codex" in invocation["harnesses"] and os.path.isfile(override) and os.path.getsize(override):
        print(f"warning: {override} is not empty and shadows the rendered AGENTS.md", file=sys.stderr)
    if not changes:
        say(f"nothing to install — every output is already in place in {home}")
        return 0, 0
    if dry_run:
        for rel, cur, want in changes:
            say(f"would {describe(rel, cur, want)}")
        say(f"dry run: {len(changes)} change(s), nothing written")
        return 0, len(changes)

    name, bdir = new_backup(home)
    entries = []
    for rel, cur, want in changes:
        e = {"path": rel, "prior": cur["type"]}
        if cur["type"] == "symlink":
            e["target"] = cur["target"]
        if cur["type"] == "file":
            e["sha256"] = cur["sha256"]
        if cur["type"] in ("file", "dir"):
            e["stored"] = "files/" + rel
        e["installed"] = {k: v for k, v in record(rel, want).items() if k != "path"} if want else {"type": "removed"}
        entries.append(e)
    write_json(os.path.join(bdir, "manifest.json"), {"backup": name, "home": home, "entries": entries})

    for (rel, cur, want), e in zip(changes, entries):
        p = os.path.join(home, rel)
        if cur["type"] == "symlink":
            os.unlink(p)
        elif cur["type"] in ("file", "dir"):
            dst = os.path.join(bdir, e["stored"])
            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
            shutil.move(p, dst)
        if want:
            create(p, want)
        say(f"  {describe(rel, cur, want)}")
    say(f"installed {len(changes)} change(s) into {home}; prior state in {bdir}")
    say(f"undo: governance restore --home {home}")
    return 0, len(changes)


def cmd_install(a):
    home = os.path.abspath(a.home)
    if not os.path.isdir(home):
        print(f"error: --home is not a directory: {home}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    invocation = {"repo": os.path.abspath(a.repo or ROOT),
                  "adapters": [os.path.abspath(p) for p in a.adapter],
                  "local": os.path.abspath(a.local) if a.local else None,
                  "harnesses": list(dict.fromkeys(a.harness or ["claude"]))}
    if a.write_manifest and len(invocation["adapters"]) != 1:
        print("error: --write-manifest records ONE adapter; this install names "
              f"{len(invocation['adapters'])}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    rc, _ = install_home(home, invocation, a.dry_run)
    if rc == 0 and a.write_manifest and not a.dry_run:
        adapter = invocation["adapters"][0]
        vault = os.path.dirname(adapter) if os.path.basename(adapter) == ADAPTER_DIR else None
        m = manifest_from(invocation["repo"], home, invocation["harnesses"], adapter, vault,
                          [vault] if vault else [], invocation["local"])
        os.makedirs(os.path.join(home, ADAPTER_DIR), exist_ok=True)
        write_json(os.path.join(home, MANIFEST), m)
        print(f"manifest written: {os.path.join(home, MANIFEST)}")
    return rc


# --- restore ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def restore_entry(home, bdir, e, notes):
    rel, p = e["path"], os.path.join(home, e["path"])
    installed = e.get("installed", {})
    aside = os.path.join(bdir + ".restored", "displaced", rel)

    def displace():
        dst = os.path.join(bdir, "displaced", rel)
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
        shutil.move(p, dst)
        notes.append(f"changed since install, moved aside: {p} → {aside}")

    if os.path.islink(p):
        if installed.get("type") != "symlink" or os.readlink(p) != installed.get("target"):
            notes.append(f"removed a symlink that differed from the install: {p} → {os.readlink(p)}")
        os.unlink(p)
    elif os.path.isdir(p):
        if not os.listdir(p):
            os.rmdir(p)
        elif e["prior"] == "missing":
            notes.append(f"left in place, holds files the install did not create: {p}")
            return
        else:
            displace()
    elif os.path.lexists(p):
        if installed.get("type") == "file" and file_sha(p) == installed.get("sha256"):
            os.unlink(p)
        else:
            displace()

    if e["prior"] == "symlink":
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)
        os.symlink(e["target"], p)
    elif e["prior"] in ("file", "dir"):
        src = os.path.join(bdir, e["stored"])
        if os.path.lexists(src):
            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)
            shutil.move(src, p)
        else:
            notes.append(f"not in the backup, cannot restore: {p}")


def cmd_restore(a):
    home = os.path.abspath(a.home)
    broot = os.path.join(home, BACKUPS)
    names = sorted(n for n in (os.listdir(broot) if os.path.isdir(broot) else []) if BACKUP_RX.match(n))
    if not names:
        print(f"error: no backup to restore in {broot}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    target = a.backup or names[-1]
    if target not in names:
        print(f"error: no unrestored backup named {target}; available: {', '.join(names)}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    notes = []
    for name in reversed([n for n in names if n >= target]):
        bdir = os.path.join(broot, name)
        manifest = os.path.join(bdir, "manifest.json")
        entries = []
        if os.path.isfile(manifest):
            with open(manifest, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                entries = json.load(fh)["entries"]
        else:
            notes.append(f"{name} has no manifest — the install stopped before touching anything")
        for e in reversed(entries):
            restore_entry(home, bdir, e, notes)
        os.rename(bdir, bdir + ".restored")
        print(f"restored {name}: {len(entries)} path(s)")
    for n in notes:
        print(n)
    return 0


# --- check --home -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def check_home(home):
    """(lines, drift count, error or None) for the install recorded in HOME."""
    try:
        state = load_state(home)
    except Refusal as e:
        return [], 0, str(e)
    if state is None:
        return [], 0, f"NOT INSTALLED  {os.path.join(home, STATE)} does not exist"
    inv = state["invocation"]
    try:
        plan = build_plan(inv["repo"], inv["adapters"], inv["local"], inv["harnesses"])
    except Refusal as e:
        return [], 0, f"cannot re-derive the install: {e}"

    lines, drift = [], 0
    recorded = {o["path"]: o for o in state["outputs"]}
    for rel, rec in recorded.items():
        cur, want, shown = inspect(home, rel), plan.outputs.get(rel), os.path.join(home, rel)
        if cur["type"] == "missing" or (rec["type"] == "dir" and not matches(home, rel, rec, cur)):
            line = f"MISSING  {shown} — re-install"
        elif rec["type"] == "file" and not matches(home, rel, rec, cur):
            line = f"EDITED BY HAND  {shown} — move the change into a layer, then re-install"
        elif rec["type"] == "symlink" and not matches(home, rel, rec, cur):
            line = f"LINK MOVED  {shown} → {cur.get('target', cur['type'])} (installed → {rec['target']}) — re-install"
        elif want is None:
            line = f"LAYERS CHANGED  {shown} is no longer produced by the layers — re-install"
        elif record(rel, want) != rec:
            line = f"LAYERS CHANGED  {shown} is stale — re-install"
        else:
            lines.append(f"in sync  {shown}")
            continue
        drift += 1
        lines.append(line)
    for rel in plan.outputs:
        if rel not in recorded:
            drift += 1
            lines.append(f"LAYERS CHANGED  {os.path.join(home, rel)} is produced by the layers but not installed — re-install")
    return lines, drift, None


def cmd_check_home(a):
    lines, drift, err = check_home(os.path.abspath(a.home))
    if err:
        print(f"error: {err}" if not err.startswith("NOT INSTALLED") else err, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    for line in lines:
        print(line)
    return 1 if drift else 0


# --- discover ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def is_vault(d, dirs, files):
    return ".obsidian" in dirs or GOV_MD in files


def vault_role(d):
    return "adapter" if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, ADAPTER_DIR, "AGENTS.md")) else "member"


def manifest_from(core, home, harnesses, adapter, adapter_vault, vaults, local):
    return {"version": 1, "core": core, "home": home, "harnesses": list(harnesses),
            "adapter": {"vault": adapter_vault, "path": adapter} if adapter else None,
            "vaults": [{"path": v, "role": vault_role(v), "name": os.path.basename(v)} for v in vaults],
            "local": local,
            "updated": datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")}


def cmd_discover(a):
    root = os.path.abspath(a.root)
    if not os.path.isdir(root):
        print(f"error: --root is not a directory: {root}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    home = os.path.abspath(a.home) if a.home else None
    if a.write and not home:
        print("error: --write needs --home: the manifest is written under it", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    installed = None
    if home:
        try:
            state = load_state(home)
        except Refusal:
            state = None
        installed = set(state["invocation"]["adapters"]) if state else set()
    repos, vaults, adapters = [], [], []
    base = root.rstrip(os.sep).count(os.sep)
    for d, dirs, files in os.walk(root):
        if ".git" in dirs or ".git" in files:
            repos.append(d)
        if is_vault(d, dirs, files):
            vaults.append(d)
        if "AGENTS.md" in files:
            parts = [p for p in ("skills", "hooks", "domains", "settings") if p in dirs]
            if parts:
                found = {"path": d, "parts": parts}
                if installed is not None:
                    found["installed"] = d in installed
                adapters.append(found)
        depth = d.rstrip(os.sep).count(os.sep) - base
        dirs[:] = sorted(x for x in dirs if not x.startswith(".") and x not in DISCOVER_SKIP) \
            if depth < a.max_depth else []
    out = {"root": root, "repos": repos, "vaults": vaults, "adapters": adapters}

    if home:
        adapter_vaults = [v for v in vaults if vault_role(v) == "adapter"]
        harnesses = [h for h in HARNESSES if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(home, "." + h))] or ["claude"]
        local = os.path.join(home, ".claude", "CLAUDE.local.md")
        av = adapter_vaults[0] if len(adapter_vaults) == 1 else None
        out["manifest"] = manifest_from(ROOT, home, harnesses, os.path.join(av, ADAPTER_DIR) if av else None,
                                        av, vaults, local if os.path.isfile(local) else None)
        out["manifest_path"] = os.path.join(home, MANIFEST)
    print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))
    if not a.write:
        return 0
    if len(adapter_vaults) != 1:
        print("refused: the manifest records ONE adapter vault; found "
              f"{len(adapter_vaults)}: {', '.join(adapter_vaults) or '(none)'}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    os.makedirs(os.path.join(home, ADAPTER_DIR), exist_ok=True)
    write_json(out["manifest_path"], out["manifest"])
    print(f"manifest written: {out['manifest_path']}")
    return 0


# --- reconcile ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def load_manifest(path):
    if not os.path.isfile(path):
        raise Refusal(f"no manifest at {path} — run discover --write first")
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            m = json.load(fh)
    except ValueError as e:
        raise Refusal(f"cannot read {path}: {e}")
    if not isinstance(m, dict) or m.get("version") != 1:
        raise Refusal(f"{path}: unsupported manifest (version {m.get('version') if isinstance(m, dict) else '?'})")
    for k in ("core", "home", "harnesses", "adapter", "vaults"):
        if k not in m:
            raise Refusal(f"{path}: manifest lacks `{k}`")
    if not m["adapter"] or not m["adapter"].get("path"):
        raise Refusal(f"{path}: manifest names no adapter — run discover --write with an adapter vault present")
    return m


def split_frontmatter(text):
    """(frontmatter body without its fences, rest) — or (None, text) when there is no frontmatter.
    '---\n' + fm + '---\n' + rest reproduces the input exactly."""
    if text.startswith("---\n"):
        end = text.find("\n---\n", 3)
        if end != -1:
            return text[4:end + 1], text[end + 5:]
    return None, text


def yaml_plain(v):
    return v if re.match(r"\A[A-Za-z0-9_./-][^#:]*\Z", v) else json.dumps(v)


def with_keys(fm, keys):
    """Frontmatter text with each managed key set; unmanaged lines are kept as they are."""
    lines = fm.split("\n")
    for k, v in keys:
        rx = re.compile(r"\A" + re.escape(k) + r":\s*(.*?)\s*\Z")
        for i, line in enumerate(lines):
            m = rx.match(line)
            if m:
                if m.group(1).strip("\"'") != v:
                    lines[i] = f"{k}: {yaml_plain(v)}"
                break
        else:
            lines.insert(len(lines) - 1 if lines and lines[-1] == "" else len(lines), f"{k}: {yaml_plain(v)}")
    return "\n".join(lines)


def with_block(body, block):
    """Body with the managed block replaced in place, or appended after a blank line."""
    b = body.find(MARK_BEGIN)
    e = body.find(MARK_END, b) if b != -1 else -1
    if b != -1 and e != -1:
        e += len(MARK_END)
        return body[:b] + block + body[e:]
    if body and not body.endswith("\n"):
        body += "\n"
    return body + ("\n" if body else "") + block + "\n"


def governance_md_text(old, keys, block):
    if old is None:
        return "---\n" + with_keys("", keys) + "---\n" + "\n" + block + "\n"
    fm, rest = split_frontmatter(old)
    if fm is None:
        return "---\n" + with_keys("", keys) + "---\n" + with_block(old, block)
    return "---\n" + with_keys(fm, keys) + "---\n" + with_block(rest, block)


def pointer_block(core, adapter_ref, role):
    return "\n".join([
        MARK_BEGIN,
        "This vault is governed by a layered instruction set. Only this block and the frontmatter keys",
        "`type`, `canonical_home`, `adapter` and `role` are managed; edit anything else freely.",
        "",
        f"- core: `{core}` — the public `governance` repository (CORE), a pinned clone; never edit it in place",
        f"- adapter: `{adapter_ref}` — the organisation's layer (ADAPTER), inside its vault, tracked by git",
        f"- this vault's role: `{role}`" + (" — it carries the adapter" if role == "adapter" else " — it carries a pointer to it"),
        "- render: `bin/governance reconcile --home \"$HOME\"` (in the core clone) rebuilds every harness home",
        "  from CORE → ADAPTER → LOCAL and refreshes this block; safe to run any time, a noop when in state",
        MARK_END])


def read_text(p):
    if not os.path.isfile(p):
        return None
    with open(p, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        return fh.read()


def write_text(p, text):
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)
    tmp = p + ".governance-tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        fh.write(text)
    os.replace(tmp, p)


def cmd_reconcile(a):
    home = os.path.abspath(a.home)
    path = os.path.abspath(a.manifest) if a.manifest else os.path.join(home, MANIFEST)
    try:
        m = load_manifest(path)
    except Refusal as e:
        print(f"error: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if not os.path.isdir(home):
        print(f"error: --home is not a directory: {home}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    adapter = m["adapter"]["path"]
    results = []

    def report(item, status, detail=""):
        results.append({"item": item, "status": status, "detail": detail})
        if not a.json:
            shown = {"fixed": "would fix" if a.dry_run else "fixed"}.get(status, status)
            print(f"{shown:<9} {item}" + (f" — {detail}" if detail else ""))

    def ensure_text(item, p, wanted):
        old = read_text(p)
        if old == wanted:
            report(item, "ok")
            return
        if not a.dry_run:
            write_text(p, wanted)
        report(item, "fixed", "created" if old is None else "updated")

    # a. adapter shape
    agents = os.path.join(adapter, "AGENTS.md")
    if os.path.isfile(agents):
        report(f"adapter {agents}", "ok")
    elif os.path.lexists(agents):
        report(f"adapter {agents}", "refused", "exists but is not a regular file")
    else:
        if not a.dry_run:
            with open(os.path.join(ROOT, "adapter-template", "AGENTS.md"), encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                write_text(agents, fh.read())
        report(f"adapter {agents}", "fixed", "created from adapter-template/AGENTS.md")
    for part in ADAPTER_PARTS:
        p = os.path.join(adapter, part)
        if os.path.lexists(p) and not os.path.isdir(p):
            report(f"adapter {p}", "refused", "exists but is not a directory")

    # b. home
    invocation = {"repo": m["core"], "adapters": [adapter], "local": m.get("local"), "harnesses": m["harnesses"]}
    if invocation["local"] and not os.path.isfile(invocation["local"]):
        invocation["local"] = None    # a local layer is optional; a missing one is not a fault
    if any(r["status"] == "refused" and r["item"].startswith("adapter ") for r in results):
        report(f"home {home}", "refused", "the adapter is not in shape")
    else:
        rc, n = install_home(home, invocation, a.dry_run, say=lambda _line: None)
        if rc != 0:
            report(f"home {home}", "refused", "install refused (see above)")
        else:
            report(f"home {home}", "fixed" if n else "ok", f"{n} change(s)" if n else "")

    # c. GOVERNANCE.md and d. CLAUDE.md, per vault
    for v in m["vaults"]:
        vp, role = v["path"], v.get("role") or vault_role(v["path"])
        if not os.path.isdir(vp):
            report(f"vault {vp}", "refused", "not a directory")
            continue
        ref = os.path.relpath(adapter, vp)
        keys = [("type", "governance"), ("canonical_home", "governance"), ("adapter", ref), ("role", role)]
        gp = os.path.join(vp, GOV_MD)
        ensure_text(f"vault {gp}", gp, governance_md_text(read_text(gp), keys, pointer_block(m["core"], ref, role)))
        cp = os.path.join(vp, CLAUDE_MD)
        old = read_text(cp)
        n = sum(1 for line in (old or "").split("\n") if line.strip() == IMPORT_LINE)
        if n == 1:
            report(f"vault {cp}", "ok")
        elif n > 1:
            report(f"vault {cp}", "refused", f"`{IMPORT_LINE}` appears {n} times; it must appear once")
        else:
            text = IMPORT_LINE + "\n" if old is None else old + ("" if old.endswith("\n") or not old else "\n") + IMPORT_LINE + "\n"
            ensure_text(f"vault {cp}", cp, text)

    # e. drift
    lines, drift, err = check_home(home)
    if a.dry_run and any(r["status"] == "fixed" and r["item"].startswith("home ") for r in results):
        report(f"drift {home}", "fixed", "would be re-installed")
    elif err:
        report(f"drift {home}", "refused", err)
    elif drift:
        report(f"drift {home}", "refused", "; ".join(line for line in lines if not line.startswith("in sync")))
    else:
        report(f"drift {home}", "ok", f"{len(lines)} output(s) in sync")

    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps({"home": home, "manifest": path, "dry_run": a.dry_run, "results": results}, indent=2))
    refused = sum(1 for r in results if r["status"] == "refused")
    fixed = sum(1 for r in results if r["status"] == "fixed")
    if not a.json:
        print(f"{'dry run: ' if a.dry_run else ''}{len(results)} item(s): {len(results) - refused - fixed} ok, "
              f"{fixed} {'to fix' if a.dry_run else 'fixed'}, {refused} refused")
    return 1 if refused else 0


# --- command line -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="governance", description=__doc__,
                                 formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="command", required=True)
    for name in ("render", "check"):
        p = sub.add_parser(name)
        if name == "render":
            p.add_argument("--out", required=True)
        else:
            target = p.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)
            target.add_argument("--out", help="check one rendered file against the layers given")
            target.add_argument("--home", help="check every output of an install against its recorded sources")
        p.add_argument("--core", help="default: this repository's core/")
        p.add_argument("--adapter", action="append", default=[], help="repeatable; later adapters win")
        p.add_argument("--local")
    p = sub.add_parser("install")
    p.add_argument("--home", required=True, help="the home directory to install into; never defaulted")
    p.add_argument("--adapter", action="append", required=True, help="repeatable; later adapters win")
    p.add_argument("--local")
    p.add_argument("--harness", action="append", choices=HARNESSES, help="repeatable; default: claude")
    p.add_argument("--repo", help="the governance checkout providing CORE; default: this repository")
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--write-manifest", action="store_true",
                   help="after installing, record core/home/harnesses/adapter/local in <home>/.governance/manifest.json")
    p = sub.add_parser("restore")
    p.add_argument("--home", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--backup", help="undo every install back to and including this one; default: the newest")
    p = sub.add_parser("discover")
    p.add_argument("--root", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--home", help="mark which adapters the install in this home uses")
    p.add_argument("--max-depth", type=int, default=4)
    p.add_argument("--write", action="store_true", help="write the proposed manifest under --home")
    p = sub.add_parser("reconcile")
    p.add_argument("--home", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--manifest", help="default: <home>/.governance/manifest.json")
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    a = ap.parse_args()

    if a.command == "check" and a.home:
        if a.core or a.adapter or a.local:
            print("error: check --home re-derives from the recorded install; do not pass layers", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        return cmd_check_home(a)
    if a.command in ("render", "check"):
        return cmd_render_or_check_out(a)
    return {"install": cmd_install, "restore": cmd_restore, "discover": cmd_discover,
            "reconcile": cmd_reconcile}[a.command](a)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
